 :label: def-inner-product
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Given two vectors 
\begin_inset Formula $\vv=(v_1,\ldots,v_n)$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\vw=(w_1,\ldots,w_n)$
\end_inset

, the *inner product* of 
\begin_inset Formula $\vv$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\vw$
\end_inset

 is the scalar
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\begin_inset Formula \[
\vv\cdot\vw = v_1 w_1 + \cdots + v_n w_n.
\]
\end_inset

:::
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
:::
\begin_inset ERT
