`matrix-A` and a vector
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\begin_inset Formula \[
\vv = \begin{pmatrix}v_1\\ \vdots\\ v_n\end{pmatrix} \in\mathbb{R}^n
\]
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
the *(matrix-vector) product* of 
\begin_inset Formula $A$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\vv$
\end_inset

 is the vector
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\begin_inset Formula \[
A\vv=\begin{pmatrix}a_{1,1}v_1 + \cdots + a_{1,n}v_n\\
\vdots\\
a_{m,1}v_1 + \cdots + a_{m,n}v_n\end{pmatrix} \in\mathbb{R}^m.
\]
\end_inset

:::
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Equivalently, we can write
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\begin_inset Formula \[
(A\vv)_i = \sum_{j=1}^n A_{i,j} v_j\quad(1\le i\le m).
\]
\end_inset

(matrix-vector)
\end_layout

