 Properties of matrix-vector multiplication For matrices 
\begin_inset Formula $A$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $B$
\end_inset

, vectors 
\begin_inset Formula $\vv$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\vw$
\end_inset

 and scalars 
\begin_inset Formula $c$
\end_inset

 the following hold whenever the expressions are defined:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
- 
\begin_inset Formula $A(\vv+\vw)= A\vv + A\vw$
\end_inset

 - 
\begin_inset Formula $A(c\vv) = c(A\vv)$
\end_inset

 - 
\begin_inset Formula $(A+B)\vv = A\vv+B\vv$
\end_inset

 - 
\begin_inset Formula $(cA)\vv = c(A\vv)$
\end_inset

 :::
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
:::
